WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.512
(wooshing)

00:00:01.512 --> 00:00:03.185
(booming)

00:00:03.185 --> 00:00:04.549
- [Evan] Jonathan has asked this question

00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:05.792
like 18 times in the chat,

00:00:05.792 --> 00:00:07.533
he really needs an
answer to this question.

00:00:07.533 --> 00:00:10.120
Jonathan I appreciate the hustle.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.203
This question if for you.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.493
How does one select
people for a diverse team

00:00:16.493 --> 00:00:19.326
which you can trust and grow with?

00:00:20.241 --> 00:00:21.536
- [Steven] Hey, Jonathan.

00:00:21.536 --> 00:00:24.793
It's a great question and
I think that is something

00:00:24.793 --> 00:00:27.949
there's no easy answers
to as an entrepreneur,

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:32.358
because I've made many
decisions, and some bad decisions

00:00:32.358 --> 00:00:34.572
over the time and I'm sure we all have.

00:00:34.572 --> 00:00:37.942
But I think this, the
smart way to answer that is

00:00:37.942 --> 00:00:41.685
obviously, you know, number
one is look for the differences

00:00:41.685 --> 00:00:43.155
you need to be successful.

00:00:43.155 --> 00:00:44.623
Be quite conscious of that in

00:00:44.623 --> 00:00:48.456
and unpick any sort of
deep bias in your mind.

00:00:49.487 --> 00:00:53.630
Then pick the individual
and the key thing is,

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:55.308
with all these things,

00:00:55.308 --> 00:00:57.744
is have to be aligned around the mission.

00:00:57.744 --> 00:01:01.231
You have to be aligned around the purpose.

00:01:01.231 --> 00:01:03.713
You know, if you want to
go into the music business

00:01:03.713 --> 00:01:05.774
and the individual doesn't like music,

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:07.190
you're going to struggle.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:11.541
THey've got to bring something,
but the most important thing

00:01:11.541 --> 00:01:15.120
is you've got the alignment
and the power of the purpose,

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.979
the sense of purpose, the
sense of passion cuz, you know,

00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:20.710
being an entrepreneur is hard
work and they're going to have

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:24.590
to work really hard to be successful.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.900
If they don't have that
fire in their belly

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.769
that you've got about your big idea,

00:01:29.769 --> 00:01:31.194
then, you know, you might as well

00:01:31.194 --> 00:01:33.325
shut the conversation down straight away.

00:01:33.325 --> 00:01:34.893
Then once they've got that, I think then

00:01:34.893 --> 00:01:36.368
you got to ask yourself,

00:01:36.368 --> 00:01:38.048
"What is the complimentary skill set?"

00:01:38.048 --> 00:01:39.069
"What's the competence?"

00:01:39.069 --> 00:01:41.571
"What's the experience that
they bring to your success?"

00:01:41.571 --> 00:01:44.515
And that's very dependent on
where you are on your journey.

00:01:44.515 --> 00:01:47.373
If it's the idea stage,
it's probably blue skies

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.531
because it's probably over a partner.

00:01:49.531 --> 00:01:52.968
If it's further down in your
sort of business journey

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:57.204
then it could be around sales,
marketing, social media,

00:01:57.204 --> 00:01:59.588
it could be a very good,
I'll say optimization,

00:01:59.588 --> 00:02:02.892
it could be, you know, what
is it you need at that stage?

00:02:02.892 --> 00:02:04.476
I think you should be very
thoughtful about that.

00:02:04.476 --> 00:02:07.395
And then the next thing is
kind of making that decision

00:02:07.395 --> 00:02:10.738
and going on with it and
then, you know, honestly,

00:02:10.738 --> 00:02:14.934
the best advice to give you
is, if you make a mistake,

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.274
make the mistake and
learn early, you know,

00:02:17.274 --> 00:02:19.203
just as we do in terms of ideas.

00:02:19.203 --> 00:02:22.608
We have a culture where we want
to encourage our colleagues

00:02:22.608 --> 00:02:25.880
to fail fast and actually,
again, at Spotify,

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.658
just a daily point, they have
sort of an ideas factory,

00:02:29.658 --> 00:02:32.926
they expect nine out of 10 ideas to fail.

00:02:32.926 --> 00:02:36.939
But one idea will be a kind of
absolute, kind of barnstorm,

00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:40.463
a ripper, and they'll be hugely successful

00:02:40.463 --> 00:02:41.848
with that one idea.

00:02:41.848 --> 00:02:44.203
But I think within the culture
of a great company, again,

00:02:44.203 --> 00:02:45.660
you want to encourage people to fail.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.288
There's no fear in failure.

00:02:48.288 --> 00:02:51.172
Ultimately if it doesn't
work out as an individual

00:02:51.172 --> 00:02:54.371
down the road then it's really
important to just sit down

00:02:54.371 --> 00:02:57.301
and be transparent or authentic
and just say, you know,

00:02:57.301 --> 00:02:59.873
"it's just kind of not working
out with you, you know,

00:02:59.873 --> 00:03:02.711
"I've made a bad hiring
decision, you know, I apologize

00:03:02.711 --> 00:03:05.422
"for that, but we just got
to be honest with ourselves."

00:03:05.422 --> 00:03:09.589
Yeah, and the great
entrepreneurs I think are always

00:03:10.575 --> 00:03:12.677
sort of focused on their business,

00:03:12.677 --> 00:03:15.099
almost to a level of
ruthlessness, but they're always

00:03:15.099 --> 00:03:17.454
very compassionate with
the people around them

00:03:17.454 --> 00:03:19.708
and very authentic about that.

00:03:19.708 --> 00:03:21.313
- I agree with everything Steven's saying.

00:03:21.313 --> 00:03:23.642
The thought that I'm
going through in my head

00:03:23.642 --> 00:03:26.512
just to add to it, is
I like testing people

00:03:26.512 --> 00:03:27.638
on different projects.

00:03:27.638 --> 00:03:32.109
I think if you can find
an easy way to get tested,

00:03:32.109 --> 00:03:33.627
so give then an assignment,

00:03:33.627 --> 00:03:35.553
so whether you're bringing on interns or

00:03:35.553 --> 00:03:37.523
whether you're in the hiring process,

00:03:37.523 --> 00:03:40.712
I'm not a big fan of the
typical job interview process,

00:03:40.712 --> 00:03:42.844
I'd rather just let them
get to work on something

00:03:42.844 --> 00:03:44.325
and see how it goes.

00:03:44.325 --> 00:03:46.796
So I'll give them five
hours to work on a project

00:03:46.796 --> 00:03:49.423
and see what comes up and be willing

00:03:49.423 --> 00:03:51.933
to be surprised and open to the ideas.

00:03:51.933 --> 00:03:55.932
If you have some kind of
way to test people out

00:03:55.932 --> 00:03:59.230
on a small, short term basis,
and again, to Steven's point,

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.292
if you're aligned on the
mission, here's our goals,

00:04:01.292 --> 00:04:03.270
here's where we're trying to get to,

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:06.199
but I'm open to how the path,
how we're going to get there,

00:04:06.199 --> 00:04:09.327
if you can find ways to work
with people and test 'em out,

00:04:09.327 --> 00:04:12.396
see what ideas might come out,
I think you'll be surprised.

00:04:12.396 --> 00:04:14.474
A lot of the people who are on my team,

00:04:14.474 --> 00:04:17.846
I have a team of misfits, like
they would have a hard time

00:04:17.846 --> 00:04:20.973
getting a job other places,
they had the worst resumes,

00:04:20.973 --> 00:04:23.640
their cover letter wasn't great,

00:04:24.782 --> 00:04:28.098
but I just gave them a
chance and they surprised me.

00:04:28.098 --> 00:04:31.793
Cuz often the skills, if
you're hiring a video editor,

00:04:31.793 --> 00:04:34.579
their cover letter doesn't
really make a big difference,

00:04:34.579 --> 00:04:36.265
I'm not hiring them for
their writing abilities,

00:04:36.265 --> 00:04:39.598
I want to know they can make great videos.

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:45.220
To Steven's point about not
falling into stereotypes

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.859
and just giving people a test,
I think you'll be surprised

00:04:48.859 --> 00:04:50.546
if you do that with enough people.

00:04:50.546 --> 00:04:51.647
(wooshing)

00:04:51.647 --> 00:04:52.730
(booming)

